109/TVCG.2024.3456207", "asserted-by": "object"}]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2025, 3, 14]], "date-time": "2025-03-14T04:19:40Z", "timestamp": 1741925980072, "version": "3.38.0"}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "SCITEPRESS - Science and Technology Publications", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2025]]}, "DOI": "10.5220/0013379900003890", "type": "proceedings-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 2, 28]], "date-time": "2025-02-28T12:43:20Z", "timestamp": 1740746600000}, "page": "1412-1418", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["A Collaborative Approach to Multimodal Machine Translation: VLM and LLM"], "prefix": "10.5220", "author": [{"given": "Amulya", "family": "Dash", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "Birla Institute of Technology and Science, Pilani, Rajasthan, India"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Yashvardhan", "family": "Sharma", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Birla Institute of Technology and Science, Pilani, Rajasthan, India"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "3171", "event": {"name": "17th International Conference on Agents and Artificial Intelligence", "start": {"date-parts": [[2025, 2, 23]]}, "location": "Porto, Portugal", "end": {"date-parts": [[2025, 2, 25]]}}, "container-title": ["Proceedings of the 17th International Conference on Agents and Artificial Intelligence"], "original-title": ["A Collaborative Approach to Multimodal Machine Translation: VLM and LLM"], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2025, 3, 13]], "date-time": "2025-03-13T12:58:06Z", "timestamp": 1741870686000}, "score": 26.67799, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.scitepress.org/DigitalLibrary/Link.aspx?doi=10.5220/0013379900003890"}}, "subtitle": [""], "issued": {"date-parts": [[2025]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.5220/0013379900003890", "published": {"date-parts": [[2025]]}}, {"institution": [{"name": "Research Square"}], "indexed": {"date-parts": [[2025, 5, 14]], "date-time": "2025-05-14T06:48:04Z", "timestamp": 1747205284110, "version": "3.40.5"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2024, 8, 12]]}, "group-title": "In Review", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Springer Science and Business Media LLC", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2024, 8, 12]], "date-time": "2024-08-12T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1723420800000}, "content-version": "unspecified", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "accepted": {"date-parts": [[2024, 8, 8]]}, "abstract": "<title>Abstract</title>\n        <p>Multimodal models integrating visual and textual data have transformed artificial intelligence applications by providing more holistic and contextually aware responses. However, the susceptibility of these models to environmental semantic distractions poses a significant challenge, as it can compromise their performance and reliability in real-world scenarios. This article evaluates the impact of semantic distractions on ChatGPT-4o and Claude 3.5 Sonnet, revealing critical vulnerabilities in their interpretative and generative capabilities. A comprehensive methodology was employed, involving the creation of controlled input variations and the systematic introduction of distractions to assess model performance. Findings indicate a substantial decline in accuracy, coherence, and consistency with increasing levels of distraction, highlighting the need for targeted improvements in model robustness. Advanced attention mechanisms, adversarial training techniques, and synthetic data augmentation are proposed as potential strategies to enhance model resilience. Despite the controlled nature of the study, the insights gained prove the importance of developing more robust multimodal models capable of maintaining high performance amidst environmental noise. Future research directions include evaluating models in more naturalistic settings and expanding the range of assessed distractions to better capture real-world complexity.</p>", "DOI": "10.21203/rs.3.rs-4880022/v1", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2024, 8, 12]], "date-time": "2024-08-12T01:58:42Z", "timestamp": 1723427922000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Evaluating the Impact of Environmental Semantic Distractions on Multimodal Large Language Models"], "prefix": "10.21203", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-0568-7044", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Simon", "family": "Kuhozido", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-0319-3740", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Graham", "family": "Dunfield", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-2682-9867", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Emily", "family": "Ostrich", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-5948-1953", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Caleb", "family": "Waterhouse", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "297", "link": [{"URL": "https://www.researchsquare.com/article/rs-4880022/v1", "content-type": "text/html", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "text-mining"}, {"URL": "https://www.researchsquare.com/article/rs-4880022/v1.html", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2024, 8, 12]], "date-time": "2024-08-12T01:58:42Z", "timestamp": 1723427922000}, "score": 26.55373, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.researchsquare.com/article/rs-4880022/v1"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2024, 8, 12]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-4880022/v1", "published": {"date-parts": [[2024, 8, 12]]}, "subtype": "preprint"}, {"institution": [{"name": "Mississippi State University", "department": ["Department of Management and Information Systems"]}], "indexed": {"date-parts": [[2022, 4, 5]], "date-time": "2022-04-05T17:00:37Z", "timestamp": 1649178037426}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Mississippi State University Libraries", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Information systems provide users with valuable information that is relevant to users\u2019 tasks, as well as irrelevant information that is not helpful to the user. Irrelevant information become a distraction and distract the users from their current task, there by impairing performance. Guided by distraction-conflict theory, processing efficiency theory, attentional control theory, cognitive load theory and memory for goals theory, this study investigated the distraction effect by exploring the research question, \u201cHow do task-irrelevant distractions interrupt the users of information systems and influence their performance?\u201d. To investigate how distractions from technology influence users\u2019 performance, this experimental research examined the relationship between the variables of distraction, cognitive load, anxiety and task performance. Data were gathered through lab experiment using imotion eye tracking system. The major findings revealed that task-irrelevant distraction negatively influenced the users by increase anxiety and cognitive load as well as increase the time devoted to primary task. We also found that the cognitive load partially mediates the relationship between distraction and time spending on task.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.54718/tgoa1959", "type": "dissertation", "created": {"date-parts": [[2022, 2, 22]], "date-time": "2022-02-22T16:24:41Z", "timestamp": 1645547081000}, "approved": {"date-parts": [[2019, 8, 9]]}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["The influence of multimodal distractions on computer user performance"], "prefix": "10.54718", "author": [{"sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Ziyi", "family": "Niu", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "12625", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2022, 2, 22]], "date-time": "2022-02-22T16:24:42Z", "timestamp": 1645547082000}, "score": 25.91349, "degree": ["Doctor of Philosophy"], "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://scholarsjunction.msstate.edu/td/5063/"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[null]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.54718/tgoa1959"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 9, 8]], "date-time": "2026-09-08T13:06:49Z", "timestamp": 1788872809141, "version": "build-2803163510"}, "edition-number": "1", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Packt Publishing", "isbn-type": [{"value": "9781835462638", "type": "electronic"}, {"value": "9781835462317", "type": "print"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}, "DOI": "10.5040/bci-0kh1.ch-010", "type": "other", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 9, 8]], "date-time": "2026-09-08T12:09:36Z", "timestamp": 1788869376000}, "page": "227-262", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Building Multimodal Applications with LLMs"], "prefix": "10.5040", "member": "2984", "container-title": ["Building LLM Powered Applications"], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 9, 8]], "date-time": "2026-09-08T12:10:13Z", "timestamp": 1788869413000}, "score": 25.216448, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.bloomsburyvisualarts.com/encyclopedia-chapter?docid=b-9781835462638&tocid=b-9781835462638-chapter10"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}, 